Use qemu-3dfx's SDL GL context backend (mglcntx_sdlgl.c, native
OpenGL.framework) instead of the GLX/XQuartz one on macOS.

XQuartz's GLX is broken on macOS Tahoe (XQuartz issue #446: Apple-DRI
opcode 129/2 BadDrawable/BadValue for any GLX client), which kills 3D
activation with "X Error of failed request: BadDrawable". Upstream ships
mglcntx_sdlgl.c with a CONFIG_DARWIN path but does not build it; both
backends export the identical symbol set. Linux keeps GLX.

--- a/hw/mesa/meson.build
+++ b/hw/mesa/meson.build
@@ -1,9 +1,10 @@
+mesa_ctx = host_os == 'darwin' ? 'mglcntx_sdlgl.c' : 'mglcntx_linux.c'
 i386_system_ss.add(files(
   'extensions_table.c',
   'mesagl_blit.c',
   'mesagl_impl.c',
   'mesapt_mm.c',
-  'mglcntx_linux.c',
+  mesa_ctx,
   'mglcntx_mingw.c',
   'mglmapbo.c',
   'mglvarry.c',
